# 70. The first headline experiment

Once this is built, I would make the first serious cross-domain Cogym result:

> **Can the same world-agnostic evolutionary laboratory optimize two structurally different problems—sequential decision-making and factual verification—without domain-specific changes to its evaluator/campaign machinery?**

Then the fact-specific result:

> **Can adaptive adversarial retrieval preserve FactJudge-level factual accuracy while materially reducing retrieval cost and latency relative to a fixed high-recall retrieval pipeline?**

That is substantially cleaner scientifically than the repo being “a trading thing, a school thing, an evolution thing, and an Alpaca hackathon variant.”

The core insight is:

> **Cogym should optimize programs/policies operating in worlds, not agents operating in markets.**

Trading was just the first organism.

Fact verification is the organism that proves Cogym actually became the lab envisioned in the Northstar.

